locked filters cause 80% of cooling and airflow issues.\n* **Inspect the outdoor unit:** Ensure there is at least 2 feet of clearance around the condenser fan.\n* **Look for error codes:** Modern appliances will display a code (e.g., CH05, E1) on the panel. Check our Error Code Database for details.\n\n> **Prime Cool Engineer\'s Tip:** Never ignore strange noises from the compressor. A rattling sound often indicates a loose mount or failing bearing, which is cheap to fix but catastrophic if ignored.\n\n## Final Verdict\n\nUltimately, your choice depends on your specific usage patterns and budget. However, we consistently recommend investing in preventative maintenance (AMC) regardless of the brand. An un-serviced premium appliance will perform worse than a well-maintained budget unit.\n\nIf you need expert assistance, the team at Prime Cool is just a call away. We specialize in rapid diagnostics and genuine OEM spare replacements.\n', 'A detailed technical comparison between Daikin and Hitachi air conditioners. We compare cooling capacity, compressor technology, ISEER ratings, and after-sales service.', '/projects/p1/ac-compressor.jpg', 'Comparisons', 'Saurav Temgire', 'Daikin vs Hitachi AC Comparison 2025 - Expert Review', 'Read our expert comparison of Daikin and Hitachi ACs. Find out which brand offers better cooling, durability, and value for money in India.', '2026-06-13T06:44:41.103Z', '2026-06-13T06:44:41.103Z'),
